---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  '@id': 'https://www.cody-peterson.com/#profilepage',
  mainEntity: { '@id': 'https://www.cody-peterson.com/#person' },
  dateCreated: '2024-01-01',
  dateModified: '2026-03-29',
};
---
<Base title="Cody Peterson" seoTitle="Cody Peterson | Depth Psychology Scholar, Author, Founder of Seba.Health" description="Published author (Chiron Publications), Jung Journal contributor, and founder of Seba.Health. Depth psychology, addiction recovery, and the ancient organ of feeling." jsonLd={jsonLd}>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <img src="/images/cody-peterson-bw.jpg" alt="Cody Peterson" class="hero-photo" width="280" height="280" />
      <div class="hero-content">
        <h1>Cody Peterson</h1>
        <p class="hero-tagline">Scholar. Author. Trickster.<br />Building something for the people nobody looks at.</p>
        <div class="hero-links">
          <a href="/book" class="btn btn-primary">The Book</a>
          <a href="https://www.seba.health" class="btn btn-outline">Seba.Health</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-epigraph">
          <span class="greek">σέβας δέ σε θυμὸν ἱκέσθω</span><br />
          "Let <em>sebas</em> reach your <em>thumos.</em>" — <em>Iliad</em> 18.178
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>The Shadow of a Figure of Light</h2>
        <p>The Archetype of the Alcoholic and the Journey to Enlightenment. Chiron Publications, 2024.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial">
        <blockquote>
          <p>"Cody Peterson has written a book whose extension is deep, wide, and high. It rests on the solid foundations of careful scholarship and personal experience, it extends the understanding of alcoholism beyond the reductive neuro-physiological explanations, and it elevates the vision of Bill Wilson and AA using the psycho-spiritual wisdom of C.G. Jung."</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="attribution">— Murray Stein, Ph.D., author of <em>The Mystery of Transformation</em></p>
      </div>
      <a href="/book" class="btn btn-primary">Read reviews & get a copy</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Published in Jung Journal</h2>
        <p>Peer-reviewed scholarship on the psychology of antiquity, emotional sobriety, and the archetype of the Alcoholic.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem;">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;"><a href="https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/19342039.2025.2487105">Taming Wild Beasts</a></h3>
          <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><em>Jung Journal: Culture & Psyche,</em> Vol. 19, Issue 2 (2025)</p>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">Iron <em>thumos</em> and the interoceptive roots of emotional sobriety in Homer's <em>Odyssey.</em></p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">The Abolished Middle (forthcoming)</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><em>Jung Journal: Culture & Psyche</em> (accepted)</p>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">The <em>tertium non datur</em> in Homer, Jung, and the recovery of the feeling function.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Seba.Health</h2>
        <p>A depth-oriented platform exploring the psychology of addiction, the roots of the psyche, and the ancient organ of feeling.</p>
      </div>
      <p>Seba.Health is the convergence of everything I've been working on: depth psychology, recovery, interoception, and the Greek concept of <em>thumos</em> — the seat of feeling that Western culture forgot. Library, glossary, essays, and a lexicon of 5,000 ancient Greek passages indexed for psychological vocabulary.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.seba.health" class="btn btn-primary">Visit Seba.Health</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
